      "content": "A distributed, low-observable signaling system utilizing orbital mechanics suggests a requirement for extreme stealth and resilience against interception. The advantage of \"communicating\" via telemetry glitches is that the signal is inherently disguised as natural physical measurement variance. This allows the system to function below the detection threshold of standard radio frequency monitoring, implying a need for secure inter-asset coordination, perhaps for tasking or status checks without alerting external observers. This points toward a sophisticated, covert operational architecture.",
